# TestNet profile (audit I-7, I-8, I-19). Three places, three owners; this file has no secrets.
# Launch order: deploy/TESTNET.md.
#
# 1) Operator machine: scripts/deploy-testnet.sh reads this file.
#    cp deploy/testnet.env.example deploy/testnet.env   (in .gitignore)
# 2) GitHub environment `testnet`: variables and secrets for deploy.yml -> release.sh (below, section 2).
# 3) Backend host: /etc/lending/ledger-credentials.env, the role accounts (deploy/testnet.credentials.env.example);
#    with real assets also LEDGER_CUSTODY_* (custodian of the EVM wallets).

# ── 1. deploy-testnet.sh ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LEDGER_NETWORK=testnet
# JSON Ledger API and gRPC Ledger API of your own TestNet participant (validator), TLS only
LEDGER_JSON_API=https://json-ledger-api.validator.example.com
LEDGER_GRPC_HOST=grpc-ledger-api.validator.example.com
LEDGER_GRPC_PORT=443
# Participant CA, if the certificate is not from a public root
#LEDGER_GRPC_CA=/path/to/ca.crt
# Tokens: 0600 files with JWTs, issued for the duration of the operation and revoked afterwards:
#   ADMIN_TOKEN_FILE     user with ParticipantAdmin: DAR upload and check (upload, check)
#   DEPLOYER_TOKEN_FILE  CanActAs operator and oracle (+ council when councilHostedHere): deployProd
#   READ_TOKEN_FILE      any user with access to /v2/packages: status
ADMIN_TOKEN_FILE=$HOME/.config/lending-testnet/admin.jwt
DEPLOYER_TOKEN_FILE=$HOME/.config/lending-testnet/deployer.jwt
READ_TOKEN_FILE=$HOME/.config/lending-testnet/reader.jwt
# Input and output of Lending.Deploy.Prod:deployProd (both in .gitignore)
DEPLOY_INPUT=deploy/testnet.deploy-input.json
DEPLOYMENT_OUT=deploy/testnet.deployment.json

# ── 2. GitHub environment `testnet` (Settings → Environments), not this file ───────────────
# Repository variables: DEPLOY_ENVIRONMENT=testnet, DEPLOY_RUNNER_LABEL=lending-testnet,
#   PUBLIC_URL=https://lend.example.com (Monitor), VITE_* for the frontend build (ci.yml).
# Environment variables:
#   LEDGER_NETWORK=testnet
#   LEDGER_API_URL=https://json-ledger-api.validator.example.com
#   PUBLIC_HOST=lend.example.com                  domain from setup.sh TLS_DOMAIN
#   BOTS=oracle,accounts,absorber,liquidator,backstop,merge,logins,indexer   (no attestation)
#   ORACLE_MODE=live
#   NETWORK_ID=canton:testnet                     wallet network (CIP-0103), checked by the frontend
#   CSP_CONNECT_SRC=https://testnet.cantonloop.com wss://testnet.cantonloop.com   Loop SDK API and WebSocket
#   CSP_MODE=report-only                          for the first week, then enforce
#   BACKEND_ENV: multi-line, KEY=VALUE, all network settings without secrets, for example:
#     SYNCHRONIZER_ID=global-domain::1220…
#     TOKEN_REGISTRY=http
#     TOKEN_REGISTRY_URLS={"usdcx":"https://…","cc":{"url":"https://…","auth":"ledger"},"cbtc":"https://…"}
#     ORACLE_SOURCES=coingecko,coinpaprika
#     RESERVE_ATTESTATION_URL=https://…
#     Real assets (ADR-005), only together and only on testnet/mainnet:
#     REAL_ASSETS=true
#     ASSET_PROFILE=real
#     EVM_WALLETS=true                              withdrawal and deposit via /evm/*; do not set without real
#     BOTS=…,deposits,redeems                       (in the BOTS variable above)
#     ETH_MIN_CONFIRMATIONS=12
#     CC_PREAPPROVAL_PROVIDER=<validator operator party>   TODO
#     XRESERVE_MAX_FEE=0                            TODO: xReserve fee
#   TEST_FAUCET: do not set, the backend will refuse to start (§7)
#   BASIC_AUTH_USER: do not set for a public launch
# Environment secrets:
#   AUTH_SECRET           openssl rand -hex 32
#   MONITOR_TOKEN         openssl rand -hex 32 (the same one in the repository Actions secrets for Monitor)
#   BACKEND_ENV_SECRETS   multi-line KEY=VALUE: API keys of price sources, etc.:
#     ETH_RPC_URL=https://sepolia…/<key>           xReserve deposit checks
#     REDSTONE_API_KEY=… KAIKO_API_KEY=… CHAINLINK_STREAMS_API_KEY=… CHAINLINK_STREAMS_API_SECRET=…
# Per-role ledger credentials do NOT go into GitHub: they live on the host (section 3).
